KNOWNBUG
nested_temporal1.sv
--liveness-to-safety --bdd
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
^\[main\.p0\] always s_eventually always main\.c != 20: PROVED$
--
--
property_supported (src/ebmc/liveness_to_safety.cpp) accepts any
"always s_eventually p", without checking that p is a state predicate.
translate_GFp then uses p in the next-state constraint of the 'live'
variable as if it were a state predicate.  With a temporal operand, the
BDD engine reports REFUTED for a property that holds; the word-level
engines fail with "instantiate_word_level got temporal operator".
Properties with temporal operands should be rejected by the translation.
